    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CT4ymBGAePbPQKB43yNg19)_\n\n- Adds `g` (global) to the per-batch prompt of `sp-batch-report-run-batches`: apply this batch and all later ones at once, nothing more asked.\n- Shared runner, so it works the same in all commands that use it:\n  - `sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all-convert`, `-parent-lint-convert`, `-title-lint-convert`\n  - `sp-vulpea-meta-order-convert`\n  - the keyword conversion of all notes\n- Dropped/excluded entries are filtered before the runner, so they stay out; each command still makes its own backups.\n- Doc updated in `docs/tangles/funct/sp-batch-report.org` (and tangled `.el`).\n- Tested with stubbed prompt in Emacs: skip batch 1, `g` on batch 2 applied the remaining 8 with no more prompts.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDEKdiiBXJEqQwZDBA)_",
